`app.js` currently contains CLI prompts, endpoint access, polling, result parsing, printing and participant prize accounting in one file.

Suggested clean-code split:
- `cli` for menu and prompts;
- `lottery-api` for endpoint calls and payload validation;
- `draw-status` for status interpretation;
- `prize-checker` for number/prize state;
- `participants` or `accounting` for shared participation calculations.

Why it matters:
- endpoint changes can be tested without interactive prompts;
- prize accounting can be tested with static fixtures;
- UI changes will not touch the integration code.

Acceptance criteria:
- `app.js` is mostly orchestration;
- endpoint parsing is isolated and testable;
- participant calculations are isolated from console rendering;
- local `npm start` behavior remains the same.

