## Problem

The existing tests cover individual functions in isolation but there is no single end-to-end integration test that walks through a complete, successful raffle lifecycle.

## Required Test

```rust
#[test]
fn full_lifecycle_happy_path() {
    let env = Env::default();
    env.mock_all_auths();
    env.ledger().set_timestamp(1000);

    // 1. Deploy factory and register raffle WASM
    // 2. Init factory
    // 3. Creator calls create_raffle
    // 4. Creator deposits prize
    // 5. Three buyers purchase tickets
    // 6. Creator calls finalize_raffle (after end time)
    // 7. Verify winner is one of the three buyers
    // 8. Advance past claim lockup
    // 9. Winner claims prize
    // 10. Verify winner's balance increased by net_prize
    // 11. Verify raffle status == Claimed
    // 12. Verify protocol fee reached treasury

    // Assert invariant: total_distributed == prize_amount - protocol_fees
}
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Test covers the complete happy path from factory init to prize claim
- [ ] Verifies token balance changes at every step
- [ ] Verifies raffle status transitions at every step
- [ ] Verifies events emitted at every step
- [ ] Test is in `contracts/raffle-instance/src/test.rs`

## Problem

The metadata_hash is committed at raffle creation and is immutable. This is good for fairness (prevents changing rules after tickets sell), but there are legitimate cases where metadata needs updating before tickets go on sale — e.g., fixing a typo in the image URL or updating the description while the raffle is in PendingPrize state.

## Design

Allow creator to update metadata_hash ONLY while no tickets have been sold and prize has not been deposited:

```rust
pub fn update_metadata_hash(env: Env, new_hash: BytesN<32>) -> Result<(), Error> {
    let mut raffle = read_raffle(&env)?;
    raffle.creator.require_auth();

    // Only before prize deposit and ticket sales
    if raffle.status != RaffleStatus::PendingPrize {
        return Err(Error::InvalidStatus);
    }
    if raffle.tickets_sold > 0 {
        return Err(Error::InvalidStatus);
    }
    if new_hash == BytesN::from_array(&env, &[0u8; 32]) {
        return Err(Error::InvalidParameters);
    }

    let old_hash = raffle.metadata_hash.clone();
    raffle.metadata_hash = new_hash.clone();
    write_raffle(&env, &raffle);

    MetadataHashUpdated { old_hash, new_hash, updated_by: raffle.creator, timestamp: env.ledger().timestamp() }.publish(&env);
    Ok(())
}
```

Metadata hash is permanently locked once prize is deposited (Active status).

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Creator can update metadata_hash in PendingPrize state
- [ ] Update is blocked once prize is deposited (Active or later)
- [ ] MetadataHashUpdated event includes old and new hash for audit trail
- [ ] Test: update hash in PendingPrize, verify update blocked after deposit_prize

